
===== n=4: m=3, classes 3 (SC 2, NS 1) =====
 (A) blue W: |W|=4=2^2 (dim 2 expected); linear(sample)=True; each SC blue-fiber ODD=True; NS blue-fiber 0=True
 (B) flip-rank: rho_all=2 (lb 2); rho_SC=1 (lb 1, #SC=2); rho_NS=0 (lb 0, #NS=1)
 (C) covering-excess: SC 0, NS 0, all 0  => bottleneck is NS/all
     T-join: SC nodes = odd-boundary of blue graph (|T|=#SC=2, even? True); SC blue-fibers odd => low-dim affine cover of SC must resolve an odd-parity partition of W

